//   span resets currentConstrainedOut to [], and the empty suffix of generated
//   matches []. Inside-close branch makes the implication vacuous by leaving the
//   constrained mode. Inside-append branch preserves the suffix relation because
//   either ConstrainedStep guarantees it directly, or AppendConstrainedToken
//   appends the same token to generated and currentConstrainedOut.
//
// cost accounting:
//   Every non-breaking branch uses exactly one cost-bumping helper and then
//   increments steps by 1: UnconstrainedStep, OpenConstrainedSpan,
//   CloseConstrainedSpan, GroupBoostedConstrainedStep together with
//   AppendConstrainedToken, or ConstrainedStep. AppendConstrainedToken itself is
//   non-bumping, so the branch's accounting comes from the preceding constrained
//   sampling helper. The returned cost is assigned from steps, hence cost <=
//   maxSteps.
//
// progress:
//   UnconstrainedStep appends exactly one token on the non-EOS path and the
//   branch increments steps by 1; on EOS it breaks immediately. Direct-open
//   appends exactly the delimiter token and increments steps by 1. Close branch
//   appends at most one token and increments steps by 1. Group-boosted inside
//   branch appends exactly one constrained token via AppendConstrainedToken and
//   increments steps by 1; fallback ConstrainedStep either breaks on EOS or
