//
// cost accounting: We return `cost := steps`, so the loop only needs to keep
//   `steps <= maxSteps`. Every non-breaking branch uses exactly one cost-
//   bumping helper: UnconstrainedStep, CloseConstrainedSpan, or
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep, and then increments steps by 1. Break branches
//   also increment steps first and then exit, so the final returned cost is the
//   number of loop iterations that consumed decoding work.
//
// progress: UnconstrainedStep appends no token on EOS or exactly one token
//   otherwise; we still do steps := steps + 1, so |generated| <=
//   |generatedPrefix| + steps remains true. CloseConstrainedSpan appends at
