//   insideConstrainedOut := false, so the implication is vacuous. In the
//   adaptive constrained branch, the helper returns either eosToken or a token
//   whose append preserves parser validity; AppendConstrainedToken then yields
//   parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
// suffix: In the unconstrained branch, when we stay outside the span the
//   implication is vacuous; when we enter on `"<<"`, currentConstrainedOut is
//   reset to [], which matches the length-0 suffix of generated. In the close
//   branch, CloseConstrainedSpan appends only the delimiter and resets the
//   tracked constrained contents to [], so the implication is again vacuous. In
//   the adaptive constrained branch, AppendConstrainedToken appends the same
//   token to both generated and currentConstrainedOut, preserving the suffix
//   equality.
// cost accounting: We return `cost := steps` at the end, and maintain the loop
//   invariant `cost == 0` throughout the loop. Every non-breaking branch uses a
//   cost-bumping helper exactly once (UnconstrainedStep, CloseConstrainedSpan,
//   or AdaptiveConstrainedStep) and then increments `steps` by 1, so the final
//   returned cost is bounded by maxSteps.
// progress: UnconstrainedStep appends exactly one token and we do
//   steps := steps + 1. CloseConstrainedSpan appends at most one token and we
//   again increment steps by 1. AdaptiveConstrainedStep itself only chooses the
//   next valid token; on non-EOS we append exactly one token with
//   AppendConstrainedToken and increment steps by 1, while on EOS we break
//   immediately after the increment. Therefore every non-breaking iteration
//   strictly increases steps and preserves |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
